fix: hero marks keep their shape, stay small, and fill the section

Three faults, one of them a real bug.

The marks looked pressed flat, and that was `preserveAspectRatio="none"`
on the SVG. It stretched a 1200x800 box to the hero's own 1440x825,
squashing every mark horizontally — they were not just small, they were
the wrong shape. The viewbox is now 1600x900, close to the hero's own
proportion, and the SVG is fitted with `slice`, which scales to cover
and crops the overflow instead of distorting it. Every mark keeps its
true geometry at any viewport.

Size is now one tight band, 7 to 11.5 units, with no exceptions. The
previous pass kept a scattering of 19-26 unit marks as focal points;
among several hundred small ones those read as mistakes rather than as
accents, so they are gone. Mark count rises from 323 to 669.

The pattern reaches the foot of the hero. A mask was fading the bottom
third to nothing on the assumption it would otherwise collide with the
photo row — but that row is a sibling section below the hero in normal
flow, so it already covers the marks where the two meet. The mask was
only leaving the hero's lower half bare. The density floor also rises,
so the left side carries texture rather than trailing off behind the
headline.

Verified: 669 marks in the DOM, the lowest sitting at 827px against a
hero ending at 825 with the carousel starting there, 3,229 pattern
pixels measured near the foot where there were none before. Below 640px
the stroke thins to 1.3 and 325 dense marks are hidden, leaving 344.
